 Ordinary Differential Operators: Vectors and Functions 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

Vectors are functions and functions are vectors 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

A vector 
\begin_inset Formula $\begin{bmatrix}x_1\\x_2\\x_3\end{bmatrix}$
\end_inset

 in 3-space is really a function 
\begin_inset Formula $x:\set{1,2,3}\rightarrow \Real$
\end_inset

 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

We just write them differently than functions, i.e., instead of 
\begin_inset Formula $x(i)$
\end_inset

 we write 
\begin_inset Formula $x_i$
\end_inset

. 
\end_layout

