 Ordinary Differential Operators: Vectors and Functions 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

And since the domain 
\begin_inset Formula $\set{1,2,3}$
\end_inset

 of the function 
\begin_inset Formula $x$
\end_inset

 is so small, we can exhibit all values of 
\begin_inset Formula $x$
\end_inset

 explicitly in one fell swoop, i.e., as 
\begin_inset Formula $\begin{bmatrix}x_1\\x_2\\x_3\end{bmatrix}$
\end_inset

 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

But, by the same token, ordinary real functions 
\begin_inset Formula $f:\Real\rightarrow\Real$
\end_inset

 are vectors 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

They just have so many components that we can't exhibit them all at once 
\end_layout

