 Ordinary Differential Operators: Vectors and Functions 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

We can add vectors by adding their components: 
\begin_inset Formula $z=x+y$
\end_inset

 if and only if 
\begin_inset Formula $z_i=x_i+y_i$
\end_inset

 for each index 
\begin_inset Formula $i$
\end_inset

 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

By the same token, we can add functions componentwise: 
\begin_inset Formula $h=f+g$
\end_inset

 if and only if 
\begin_inset Formula $h(t)=f(t)+g(t)$
\end_inset

 for all 
\begin_inset Formula $t$
\end_inset

 in the domain 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

Componentwise multiplication of functions can also be defined (although this does not come up as often for ordinary vectors): 
\begin_inset Formula $h=f\cdot g$
\end_inset

 if and only if 
\begin_inset Formula $h(t)=f(t)\cdot g(t)$
\end_inset

 for all 
\begin_inset Formula $t$
\end_inset

 in the domain 
\end_layout

