 Ordinary Differential Operators: Differentiable Functions 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

Let 
\begin_inset Formula $I=[a,b]$
\end_inset

 be any closed interval of the real line 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

Consider the set 
\begin_inset Formula $\Real^I=\set{f:I\rightarrow \Real}$
\end_inset

 of all functions mapping 
\begin_inset Formula $I=[a,b]$
\end_inset

 into the real numbers 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

Then, as we have just pointed out, 
\begin_inset Formula $\Real^I$
\end_inset

 is a vector space over the reals 
\end_layout

