\begin_layout Itemize

This operation turns out to be a linear operator on the vector space of functions that are differentiable on 
\begin_inset Formula $I=[a,b]$
\end_inset

. 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

In fact, we want to consider those functions that can be differentiated as many times as we like 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

Thus, we consider the space of infinitely differentiable, real-valued functions defined on the closed real interval 
\begin_inset Formula $[a,b]$
\end_inset

: 
\begin_inset Formula $C^\infty[a,b]$
\end_inset

 
\end_layout

