 Ordinary Differential Operators 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

Since the derivatives of all orders are assumed to exist for all functions 
\begin_inset Formula $f\in C^\infty[a,b]$
\end_inset

, the limit of the difference quotient always exists for such functions. 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

Thus, we assign to each 
\begin_inset Formula $f$
\end_inset

 a new function 
\begin_inset Formula $Df$
\end_inset

 given by 
\begin_inset Formula \begin{equation}\label{deriv}
  [Df](t) = \lim_{s\rightarrow t}\frac{f(s)-f(t)}{s-t}
\end{equation}
\end_inset

 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

This assignment defines a transformation 
\begin_inset Formula \[D:C^\infty[a,b]\rightarrow C^\infty[a,b]\]
\end_inset

 that is a linear operator. 
\end_layout

